udept Authors
=============

Original author (2004-2007, SVN era):

    Ed Catmur <ed@catmur.co.uk>

Modernization (0.6.0 onwards):

    istitov/udept                   https://github.com/istitov/udept
        Ivan S. Titov <iohann.s.titov@gmail.com> — modernization
        pass against current Portage on top of the init-6 import:
        modern atoms, md5-cache, BDEPEND/IDEPEND, virtuals/*
        category, EROOT, the test infrastructure (bats + smoke
        harness), slot-aware revdep filtering, the REQUIRED_USE
        evaluator, and zsh completion. See the 0.6.0 and 0.7.0
        entries in ChangeLog for the per-release detail.

        The 0.6.0 and 0.7.0 work was carried out with heavy use of
        the Claude large-language model (Anthropic) as a coding
        assistant; every change was reviewed by hand and validated
        against the bats unit suite and the smoke-harness regression
        net before landing.

Forks whose work was incorporated:

    init-6/udept                    https://gitlab.com/init-6/udept
        Andrey Ovcharov <sudormrfhalt@gmail.com> imported Ed's 2006
        SVN codebase to git, applied two queued gentoo-bugzilla
        patches that never went upstream (default-use, bug #172611
        comment 9; svn-1638, bug #172611 comment 10), fixed
        make.conf location handling, and made misc cleanups. The
        init-6 branch was the immediate ancestor of this repo's
        modernization line — without it the 2006 codebase would
        have been even harder to pick up.

Other forks reviewed but with no commits incorporated:

    lkraav/udept                    https://github.com/lkraav/udept
        A separate community fork from the dormant period;
        reviewed for overlapping work but the modernization pass
        took its own path.

See ChangeLog for per-release contributor detail and README.md for
project context.
